ready: 1
kind: rule
id: recall.rule.session-index
display_id: RULE-RECALL-SESSION-INDEX
module: recall
title: What the session-start index lists
summary: The session index lists pointers to the memories most likely to matter before the first prompt, within its budget.
table:
  columns: [order, group, ordering inside the group]
  rows:
    - ["1", Boot settings and the active self-narrative, as saved]
    - ["2", Protected memories and values, by priority]
    - ["3", Guardrails then preference beliefs, by strength times salience]
    - ["4", Where you left off, the latest checkpoint]
    - ["5", Active goals and open questions, newest first and at most five]
    - ["6", Playbooks as name and one-line description, by strength times salience]
    - ["7", Other memories, by the working-memory score]
default: When the next line does not fit, stop and add one line saying how many more memories the recall tool can find
rules:
  - recall.rule.priority
constants:
  - recall.const.session-index-budget
rationale: >-
  Guardrails and preferences come early because they change behavior before the
  first prompt; a guardrail that arrives after the risky step is too late. The
  index is a list of pointers, not full memories, so the agent's work keeps most
  of its context and any memory can be read on demand.
